# The commit of qoryai/integrations that every integrations contract in this repository
# is copied from, byte for byte. `test/apiary/contract_copies_test.exs` checks each copy
# against `test/fixtures/contract-copies.sha256`, the SHA-256 of each file at this commit.
#
# contracts/integration/v1 is copied to three places:
# - its schemas and README.md, to test/fixtures/contract/integration/v1/,
# - connect-return.schema.json and setup-pass.schema.json, to
#   test/fixtures/integration-contract/schema/,
# - its fixtures/ folder, to test/fixtures/integration-contract/: the description
#   fixtures, accepted, refused under invalid/, refused by a reader under
#   refused-by-reader/, and the documents that only a closed copy of a schema refuses
#   under closed/; and under adapter/ the fixtures of each request, answer and report
#   of the adapter contract.
#
# description.schema.json, definitions.schema.json, changes.schema.json (which
# Apiary.Adapters.ChangeRequest checks an entry against), changes-submitted.schema.json
# and changes-failed.schema.json (which Apiary.Adapters.ChangeReport checks a report
# against) are copied to priv/contract/integration/ too, and the data descriptions of
# model providers, descriptions/*.json at the repository's root, to
# priv/contract/integration/descriptions/.
#
# The run, explore, diagnostics and provisioner contracts, documents-check and the run
# contract's documents.schema.json beside Apiary.Stacks.Document are copied from the same
# commit: see `.contract-ref` in each of those folders.
#
# Apiary holds the bounds of a description: the 256 KiB of a fetched description.json
# when it is fetched, and every bound, those 256 KiB included, in
# Apiary.Integrations.Description.parse/1, which an adapter's start-up gives the
# description's value as its body carries it. The schema checks the shape of each `links`
# entry. Apiary does not check that each system is listed once or that the host of a
# template is its system, which integrations' `contracts.CheckLinks` checks.
